      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): handle stdout/stderr stream errors in find tool",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `find` tool spawns `fd`/`find` and reads stdout/stderr through a `readline` interface. If either stream emits an error before or during line processing, the error is not handled, which can crash the agent process with an unhandled exception. The child process may also be left running after the error.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMirror the fix already applied to `bash` (#101005) and `grep` (#101014): attach explicit error handlers to both the readline interface and the raw stdout/stderr streams. On a stream error the child is now terminated before the tool rejects, so transient stream failures are logged, the tool result reflects the failure, and no orphan `fd` process remains.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAgent runs using the `find` tool are more resilient to OS-level stream failures (e.g., pipe errors, resource limits).\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Updated regression tests in `src/agents/sessions/tools/find.fd.test.ts` to assert that the child is killed when stdout or stderr emits an error.\n- Added a real behavior proof script at `scripts/proof/find-tool-stream-errors.mts` that places a fake `fd` on PATH, forces stdout/stderr stream errors, and verifies the tool rejects cleanly and the child is killed.\n\nLocal verification:\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/sessions/tools/find.fd.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests  5 passed (5)\n\n$ OPENCLAW_OXLINT_SKIP_PREPARE=1 node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs src/agents/sessions/tools/find.ts src/agents/sessions/tools/find.fd.test.ts scripts/proof/find-tool-stream-errors.mts\nFound 0 warnings and 0 errors.\n\n$ node --import tsx scripts/proof/find-tool-stream-errors.mts\n=== Proof: find tool stream error catch ===\n\nRejected as expected: fd stdout error: stdout read failed\n\nPASS: find tool caught stream errors and killed the child process.\n```",
        "branch": "fix/find-tool-stream-errors",
